SN LunarStats v1.1

Generates the current moon phase, it's age in days and the date of the next
full moon (peak).  Runs once nightly and creates a textfile for viewing in
a bulletin menu, GFiles or anything else you can think of.

Quick & Easy Installation:

 1  Place it somewhere.  (PFiles: would be good.)

 2  Add the following event:

    COMMAND:  RunARexx
    ARGS:     SN:SN_LunarStats (provide correct path)
    PORT(S):  0 (or whatever your maintenance port is)
    TYPE:     Immediate - system idle or not
    MM/DD:    SSMTWTF
    TIME:     0 (or as close to midnight as possible)
    VALID:    1
    INTERVAL: 0
    ITERATE:  1

    When this event runs, it creates a file called "_LunarStats" in the
    directory the program file is run from.

 3  Add the output textfile to either a Bulletin Menu program of your
    choosing or directly into GFiles and you're all done!

(This sucker wasn't big enough to deserve it's own .guide, installer, icons,
help file, blah blah blah plus tax...)

Midnight

